{
  "summary": "Final acceptance pass on the dashboard auth/secrets/settings work: added admin reconciliation for uncertain bookings (Mark confirmed / Mark not booked — pure record-keeping, never calls Google), a safe offline master-key rotation script (npm run rotate-master-key), and a 'Log out everywhere' session-revoke action. Verified docker compose config (daemon still unavailable in this environment, marked unverified honestly). Ran a full live browser audit of every dashboard section including seeding and reconciling two real uncertain bookings end-to-end. Confirmed webhook/health/readiness regressions clean.",
  "nextSteps": "Only legitimate external setup remains: real Meta/WhatsApp Business credentials + webhook registration, a real OpenRouter API key, a real Google service-account + calendar share, a real DOMAIN for Caddy/HTTPS, and (when a Docker-capable environment is available) an actual docker compose build/up verification. No further internal engineering work is outstanding against the explicit scope of this task.",
  "tests": "npm test: 36 files, 249 tests passed (up from 233) — new: bookingLockRepo reconciliation guards (confirmed/not-booked transitions, no-op on wrong state, slot freed for retry), destroyAllSessions unit test, a master-key-rotation round-trip test (old key fails post-rotation, new key recovers exact plaintext), and dashboard integration tests for the reconcile endpoint (400/409/200) and logout-all (revokes both the caller's and a second session). npm run typecheck/lint/build all passed. Live browser audit: seeded two real uncertain booking_locks rows via a throwaway script, verified 'Mark not booked' actually deletes the row and frees the slot for a fresh claim, verified 'Mark confirmed' actually records the admin-supplied event id and flips status to confirmed, verified 'Log out everywhere' actually forces re-login, all with zero console errors and the server staying up throughout. Regression-checked signed webhook (200)/bad-signature (401)/health/readiness/unauthenticated-401 all still correct. docker compose config validates cleanly (healthcheck + depends_on:condition:service_healthy parse correctly); docker build/up/migration/volume-persistence remain UNVERIFIED — the Docker Desktop Linux engine is unavailable in this environment, stated honestly rather than faked.",
  "lastHandoff": "handoffs/1064caee-f2bf-45b5-b4ed-9f47ff7a7810-079394ea-4465-46f8-a08a-f446b1b1c301.json",
